+## XIV.1a Source-enforced failure settlement (3 November 2026)
+
+The all-necessary mechanism and its energy collateral are retained. The next
+increment supplies the queued founding-side adversarial counterpart for the
+**admitted failure-settlement epoch**: the executable
+`PhysicalBridges.AnchorPledgeForfeiture` controller and
+`Snuffy.FoundingEscrowBridge`.
+
+Each immutable ticket carries its recipient, full refund, failure bonus and
+complete service charge. `commit` admits a queue only when the bond, cash
+liability and service work are funded; `accepted_commit_certificate` derives
+the source readiness and exact initial ledger from acceptance. Arbitrary
+adaptive anchor requests can withdraw only free stock or trigger forfeiture
+of the posted bond. They cannot cancel the queue, rewrite a ticket or release
+its reserves. Every funded nonterminal tick automatically settles its next
+full ticket. `funded_failure_settles_every_claim` proves completion after the
+initial queue length in ticks, with the full paid-ticket history retained.
+Every prefix remains funded and conserves the complete accounted ledger;
+processed breach zeroes the bond and forfeiture never decreases at later
+prefixes.
+
+The original complete activation bill is itemised, not enlarged:
+\(d=a+\sum_{i\in N}w_i\), with a already charged before this settlement
+epoch and w_i the complete reserved service charges. From the same original
+collateral bound \(A+d+\sum_{i\in N}b_i\le R\),
+`every_subset_has_source_guarantee` constructs an accepted source for every
+actual contributor subset S. Received pledges stay refundable and are not
+bonus income. `collateral_backed_all_necessary` composes this source guarantee
+with the existing pivotal dominance comparison, with no anchor-cooperation
+premise in the settlement theorem. The deterministic sorted registry gives
+unique recipient tickets and unique recipients in every paid prefix.
+
+This increment adds 44 checked statements; the fresh canonical closure is
+nine modules / 68 audited statements. The separate physical package builds
+the byte-identical controller and exercises all 27 three-request paths,
+including paid service work and underfunded rejection. The whole source epoch
+is specified here: actual campaign registration, incoming-pledge metering,
+first commitment/pre-failure custody, default trigger, controller/export and
+external-effect binding, physical recipient transfers, tick timing and
+complete calibrated service costs remain the standing source/installation
+correspondences. General sensor coverage and actual commissioning are not
+closed by this source program. No protected mind is removed from the domain.
